{"data":{"allProjectsJson":{"sections":[{"button":{"label":"Visit Github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/","visible":true},"projects":[{"category":"MOBILE APP","description":"SingWithMe is the full realization of an idea I've been chasing since my first React project. It's a mobile app that helps casual singers improve by combining vocal isolation, key/tempo shifting, and synchronized lyrics, all powered by AI. The backend uses Firebase Cloud Functions and Google Cloud Run to run Demucs for vocal separation and OpenAI Whisper for transcription. I built it with Expo and TypeScript, designed it with a sleek dark theme and neon highlights, and shipped it to both the App Store and Google Play using EAS, Fastlane, and the respective consoles. It brings together my passions for music, software engineering, and AI into one polished product.","image":{"alt":"SingWithMe App","linkTo":"https://www.singwithme.app/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/c74cd/singwithme-app.png","srcSet":"/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/52178/singwithme-app.png 100w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/bd93f/singwithme-app.png 200w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/c74cd/singwithme-app.png 400w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/c5d84/singwithme-app.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/92b20/singwithme-app.webp 100w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/ab2cb/singwithme-app.webp 200w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/4ebbf/singwithme-app.webp 400w,\n/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/af6dc/singwithme-app.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":355}},"publicURL":"/static/649ea8e7eaa121522bfd69215c9cd7e3/singwithme-app.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://www.singwithme.app/"}],"tags":["React Native","Expo","TypeScript","Firebase","Cloud Functions","Demucs","OpenAI Whisper","iOS","Android","EAS","Docker","Microservices","App Store Connect","Google Play Console","Google Cloud Console","Python","Serverless"],"title":"SingWithMe","visible":true},{"category":"OPEN SOURCE LIBRARY","description":"I needed an audio API for my Expo app with multi-track mixing and time/pitch shifting. On iOS, AVAudioEngine made this straightforward. On Android, there's no native advanced audio API. My only option was a professional SDK like Superpowered, costing thousands per year and total overkill for my needs. So I built Sezo Audio Engine. It includes two packages: an Android engine written in C++ published to JitPack, and an Expo module combining the Android engine with native iOS implementation, published to npm. Open sourced to save other developers time and money","image":{"alt":"Sezo Audio Engine","linkTo":"https://sepzie.github.io/SezoAudioEngine/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/076eb/sezo.png","srcSet":"/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/36c82/sezo.png 100w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/c2d1d/sezo.png 200w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/076eb/sezo.png 400w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/598b6/sezo.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/5d5b6/sezo.webp 100w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/ed6e6/sezo.webp 200w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/7bebf/sezo.webp 400w,\n/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/cb36b/sezo.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":315}},"publicURL":"/static/e47403fce02ae7dd72e445466cebf7cb/sezo.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://sepzie.github.io/SezoAudioEngine/"},{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/SezoAudioEngine"}],"tags":["C++","Kotlin","Swift","Expo","React Native","Android","iOS","Audio","npm","JitPack"],"title":"Sezo Audio Engine","visible":true},{"category":"INDUSTRY PROJECT","description":"ODEN was a large-scale collaborative effort to make open data more accessible. I worked in a team of 19, contributing to both the full-stack team and the tooling team. On the full-stack side, I built features using React, JavaScript, Google Cloud Functions, and a SQL database. On tooling, I helped create data pipelines along with validation and sanitization utilities. Working with such a large, cross-functional team was a great exercise in communication and coordination.","image":{"alt":"ODEN Open Data Developer Network","linkTo":"https://github.com/OpendataDeveloperNetwork/ODEN-Client","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/0e16b/oden.png","srcSet":"/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/b66ef/oden.png 100w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/bf2fb/oden.png 200w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/0e16b/oden.png 400w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/2881f/oden.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/5a717/oden.webp 100w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/99232/oden.webp 200w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/a807e/oden.webp 400w,\n/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/8225e/oden.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":276}},"publicURL":"/static/6302701382cbe68e514428afe37c3901/oden.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://terratap-oden-client-v2.web.app/"},{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/OpendataDeveloperNetwork/ODEN-Client"}],"tags":["React","JavaScript","Google Cloud Functions","SQL","Data Pipelines"],"title":"ODEN - Open Data Developer Network","visible":true},{"category":"TERM PROJECT","description":"An object detection system using YOLOv5 to identify safety helmets in images and video streams for workplace safety monitoring. Features model training on custom datasets, real-time detection via webcam, and deployment support for NVIDIA Jetson Nano edge devices.","image":{"alt":"Safety helmet detection demo showing YOLOv5 predictions","linkTo":"https://github.com/Sepzie/yolo-safety-helmet-detection","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/72fca/helmet-detection.png","srcSet":"/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/6cb8d/helmet-detection.png 100w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/e68a7/helmet-detection.png 200w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/72fca/helmet-detection.png 400w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/f6992/helmet-detection.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/64a37/helmet-detection.webp 100w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/cb817/helmet-detection.webp 200w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/d603c/helmet-detection.webp 400w,\n/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/9298b/helmet-detection.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":267}},"publicURL":"/static/1f5d795077e4020c2ce6777ae7f8d8bb/helmet-detection.jpg"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/yolo-safety-helmet-detection"}],"tags":["Python","PyTorch","Docker","YOLOv5","Computer Vision","Jetson Nano"],"title":"YOLO Safety Helmet Detection","visible":true},{"category":"PERSONAL PROJECT","description":"AI System Designer is a web app for AI-assisted system design with project workspaces, streaming chat, and generated assets like Markdown and Mermaid diagrams. It supports RAG-style context assembly, rate limits, and alerting for a production-ready workflow.","image":{"alt":"AI System Designer Screenshot","linkTo":"https://systems-designer-ai.vercel.app/login","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/9011e/system-designer-ai.png","srcSet":"/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/32719/system-designer-ai.png 100w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/bd497/system-designer-ai.png 200w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/9011e/system-designer-ai.png 400w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/79276/system-designer-ai.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/3be0b/system-designer-ai.webp 100w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/a59e2/system-designer-ai.webp 200w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/1d714/system-designer-ai.webp 400w,\n/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/a6924/system-designer-ai.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":188}},"publicURL":"/static/2fa5f88603cc3ddb869bdbee1c449039/system-designer-ai.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://systems-designer-ai.vercel.app/login"},{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/SystemsDesignerAI"}],"tags":["Next.js","React","TypeScript","Tailwind","Supabase","PostgreSQL","Vercel","LangChain","OpenAI","RAG","Cypress","Docker"],"title":"AI System Designer","visible":true},{"category":"PERSONAL PROJECT","description":"This was my first React project and the very first version of SingWithMe. It lets you break a song into individual lines with synchronized lyrics, so you can practice one segment at a time. You listen, record yourself, and compare. A simple loop that helped me improve my own singing. I built it to scratch my own itch, and it turned out to be a great way to learn React.","image":{"alt":"Sing With Me Screenshot","linkTo":"https://sepzie.github.io/sing-with-me-react/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/d6b55/singwithme.png","srcSet":"/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/1681a/singwithme.png 100w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/e1883/singwithme.png 200w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/d6b55/singwithme.png 400w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/17190/singwithme.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/81924/singwithme.webp 100w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/e8411/singwithme.webp 200w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/1c7e1/singwithme.webp 400w,\n/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/c71a2/singwithme.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":227}},"publicURL":"/static/ae4ea2be108e8573caaaa5696399e558/singwithme.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/sing-with-me-react/"},{"type":"external","url":"https://sepzie.github.io/sing-with-me-react/"}],"tags":["React","JavaScript","Web Audio API"],"title":"Sing With Me (React)","visible":true},{"category":"HACKATHON","description":"Developed a full-stack trip monitoring dashboard for a mining company as part of a 6-person team during a QDS hackathon. Analyzed big data and presented conclusions and predictions in an easy-to-use web interface. Implemented a REST API using Flask and Python and utilized Google Maps API to create a heatmap of truck locations. A data-driven solution for real-time trip monitoring.","image":{"alt":"Trip Monitoring Dashboard Screenshot","linkTo":"https://github.com/Sepzie/EnviLabs-Hackathon","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/014cf/tripmonitor.png","srcSet":"/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/78b85/tripmonitor.png 100w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/2fcc9/tripmonitor.png 200w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/014cf/tripmonitor.png 400w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/654c7/tripmonitor.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/e27c8/tripmonitor.webp 100w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/c4748/tripmonitor.webp 200w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/141f2/tripmonitor.webp 400w,\n/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/b0042/tripmonitor.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":348}},"publicURL":"/static/069df5166be6929f42f8bcc8cf906e46/tripmonitor.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/EnviLabs-Hackathon"}],"tags":["React","Flask","Python","REST API","Google Maps API","Data Analysis"],"title":"Trip Monitoring Dashboard","visible":true},{"category":"COURSE PROJECT","description":"Collaborated with a three-person team to build a Kotlin-based Android game inspired by Flappy Bird. Implemented MVVM to separate game logic from UI, a navigation graph with multiple fragments for smooth menu flow, and Firestore authentication plus leaderboard storage. Built core gameplay systems including frame-by-frame rendering and collision detection.","image":{"alt":"Sky Surfer gameplay demo","linkTo":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Sepzie/COMP3717-Android-Term-Project/refs/heads/main/sky_surfer_demo.gif","src":{"childImageSharp":null,"publicURL":"/static/5f7b7374021e003d37857cbccb6008c0/sky-surfer-demo.gif"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/COMP3717-Android-Term-Project"}],"tags":["Kotlin","Android","MVVM","Firebase","Game Development"],"title":"Sky Surfer","visible":true},{"category":"PERSONAL PROJECT","description":"CogniEasy is a lightweight GPT-powered tool that turns your resume and a job description into a polished, tailored cover letter. Built by a two-person team, it streamlines the application process with a clean, fast workflow.","image":{"alt":"CogniEasy Screenshot","linkTo":"https://innovatech-labs.github.io/cogni-easy/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/2f758/cogni-easy.png","srcSet":"/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/abfec/cogni-easy.png 100w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/5d7a7/cogni-easy.png 200w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/2f758/cogni-easy.png 400w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/029ca/cogni-easy.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/f7d31/cogni-easy.webp 100w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/81a41/cogni-easy.webp 200w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/46fc9/cogni-easy.webp 400w,\n/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/a8f18/cogni-easy.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":244}},"publicURL":"/static/13d8c0d14df4a14458d9eaba0cab37dc/cogni-easy.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://innovatech-labs.github.io/cogni-easy/"},{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/orgs/innovatech-labs/repositories"}],"tags":["React","Python","OpenAI","Docker"],"title":"CogniEasy","visible":true},{"category":"CONTRACT PROJECT","description":"This was my first real-world contract work. A friend of mine was starting up his car dealership; he had a neatly designed website built with GoDaddy's website builder, but was missing an inventory feature. I recruited my friend and classmate and we created the inventory manager using React and Firebase in a couple of months. It nicely fit the theme of the business's website, and I embedded it using an iframe. The business stopped using it as they no longer needed the inventory feature, but the whole thing is still functional, complete with an admin dashboard for adding and editing cars.","image":{"alt":"Inventory Manager Screenshot","linkTo":"https://lively-kitten-05fcac.netlify.app/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/8a6bd/inventory-manager.png","srcSet":"/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/4c424/inventory-manager.png 100w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/01e3b/inventory-manager.png 200w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/8a6bd/inventory-manager.png 400w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/2d819/inventory-manager.png 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/322f8/inventory-manager.webp 100w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/93b70/inventory-manager.webp 200w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/603a5/inventory-manager.webp 400w,\n/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/a75dd/inventory-manager.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":294}},"publicURL":"/static/8cb25b90434ece843da3cda4268d613d/inventory-manager.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"external","url":"https://lively-kitten-05fcac.netlify.app/"},{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/InventoryManager"}],"tags":["React","JavaScript","Firebase"],"title":"Inventory Manager","visible":true},{"category":"HACKATHON","description":"Outliner is a Discord bot that answers questions from BCIT course outlines using the OpenAI Answers API. Before ChatGPT and the official release of GPT-3, OpenAI was offering these more basic AI APIs and I couldn't wait to get some hands-on experience with them. So at nwHacks 2022, my team of four and I combined web scraping with a Discord bot server to create an AI chatbot with full knowledge of our course outlines. Of course, we didn't hesitate to ask it about the meaning of life; and it did not disappoint.","image":{"alt":"Trip Monitoring Dashboard Screenshot","linkTo":"https://github.com/Sepzie/OutlinerBot/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/e8044/outliner.jpg","srcSet":"/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/51e1c/outliner.jpg 100w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/b3172/outliner.jpg 200w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/e8044/outliner.jpg 400w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/a09fe/outliner.jpg 800w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/e52fc/outliner.webp 100w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/e8411/outliner.webp 200w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/a29e4/outliner.webp 400w,\n/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/64466/outliner.webp 800w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":225}},"publicURL":"/static/e0edf516073dfd6e5aaf719af3e2fb83/outliner.jpg"},"objectFit":null},"video":{"embedUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/D7p9ACDbYbA","title":"Outliner Discord Bot demo"},"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/OutlinerBot/"}],"tags":["Python","OpenAI","Web Scraping","Discord Bot"],"title":"Outliner Discord Bot (nwHacks2022)","visible":true},{"category":"COURSE PROJECT","description":"Virtual Learning Buddy (VLB) was my first introduction to web app style projects. I worked in a group of three to create a prototype of what the learning platform of the future would look like, with all the student's needs gathered in one place. We used Bootstrap for the styling, but the whole thing was still a vanilla web stack project. Little did I know this would be the last time I ever touched vanilla instead of frameworks.","image":{"alt":"Virtual Learning Buddy Screenshot","linkTo":"https://github.com/Sepzie/1800_DTC04","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/1c217/vlb.png","srcSet":"/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/f2bc9/vlb.png 100w,\n/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/6ce5d/vlb.png 200w,\n/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/1c217/vlb.png 400w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/6c57c/vlb.webp 100w,\n/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/ffc66/vlb.webp 200w,\n/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/c5eef/vlb.webp 400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":500}},"publicURL":"/static/6af5651852cea5923db118c1eb305d7e/vlb.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/1800_DTC04/"}],"tags":["HTML","CSS","JavaScript","Bootstrap","Firebase"],"title":"Virtual Learning Buddy","visible":true},{"category":"COURSE PROJECT","description":"Arena of Blood was my very first individual project when starting the Computer Systems Technology diploma. I created a text-based RPG adventure game using Python, complete with a full unit test suite for every function and comprehensive Python-style documentation. I remember getting carried away with this one when writing the story. It's definitely still worth a play. Can you find the secret ending without looking at the code?","image":{"alt":"Arena of Blood Screenshot","linkTo":"https://github.com/Sepzie/ArenaOfBlood/","src":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/ab759/arenaofblood.png","srcSet":"/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/59114/arenaofblood.png 100w,\n/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/e345d/arenaofblood.png 200w,\n/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/ab759/arenaofblood.png 400w","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/65515/arenaofblood.webp 100w,\n/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/692fe/arenaofblood.webp 200w,\n/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/3dbde/arenaofblood.webp 400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"}]},"width":400,"height":192}},"publicURL":"/static/2a994714ee103e69fd29b0a8d7248c2b/arenaofblood.png"},"objectFit":null},"video":null,"links":[{"type":"github","url":"https://github.com/Sepzie/ArenaOfBlood/"}],"tags":["Python","Unit Testing","CLI","Game Development"],"title":"Arena of Blood","visible":true}]}]}}}